  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Western Africa - Multicountry Western Africa HI (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Western Africa HI, HIV, Handicap International Federation (HI). The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To improve the availability of data on the vulnerability of people living with disabilities to HIV infection in each of the target countries.  Objective 2: To strengthen the technical and organizational capacities of civil society organizations, thereby enabling them to advocate for the inclusion of people living with disabilities in HIV/AIDS control efforts at the national and regional levels.  Objective 3: To strengthen the involvement of disability associations in the design, implementation and monitoring and evaluation of HIV/AIDS control policies and programs at the national and regional levels, so that such policies and programs better reflect the needs of people living with disabilities.  Objective 4: To encourage disability stakeholders and HIV stakeholders in West Africa to establish partnerships to develop a robust, sustainable voluntary sector</narrative>
  </description>
